Z||000004||Alex4mula||08-23-2001||09:43 AM||||I bet it will be worst than stock. It will be sucking very hot air from near the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||08-23-2001||09:51 AM||||It looks kinda cool in the compartment, but I agree with everyone else.  Hot air, cheap hardware store themal coating, go for a K&N- or better yet just get a nice chrome pipe and build your own! The chrome will look way better than the red will.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000006||gargoyle||08-23-2001||11:00 AM||||I'll admit I looked at this once before but I have to agree with everybody else. I think it would be worse than stock because of the air temp. Just drop in a K&N. I've always ran K&Ns in everything, they work great in in the stock location. You may not see it but at least it breathing outside air. ||||reg||13
Z||000007||Alex4mula||08-23-2001||11:13 AM||||Where can you get the chrome pipe?||||reg||1
Z||000008||MontanaFiero||08-23-2001||12:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Alex4mula:<BR><B>Where can you get the chrome pipe?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>well...I suppose you'd have to make it yourself, but it would be noisy and not worth it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||MinnGreenGT||08-23-2001||12:12 PM||||If you want to just buy one straight out, go with either WestCoastFiero or the Fiero Store. Both have crome cold-air intakes available and both run about $150+.  Otherwise, you can search the forum for info on how people made their own (search for "cold air intake").  I guess any metalshop or muffler shop can custom bend the pipe for you for a few bucks, then have it chromed (or powdercoated... I wonder what that would look like...?).  Anyway- many people don't think that the Cold-Air intake does anything, but I think it's worth the appearance alone.  The general idea is to get the filter out of the engine compartment-preferably into the vented area in front of the Left-Rear wheel (quarter panel) where it will collect cooler air. It tends to be more difficult to change the filter then, but someday soon I'll do it myself!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
